                [
                    "Functional Description",
                    "DW-003 is a cross-platform hardware abstraction layer and diagnostic interface module applicable to multiple Argonaut configurations. The XPHADIM module"
                ]
            ],
            "lower_row_ss": [
                [
                    "",
                    "provides a unified hardware abstraction interface that enables the ATLAS-RT operating system and VMS application software to operate across different Argonaut hardware variants (including the Argonaut-A and Argonaut-C target platforms) without requiring platform-specific source-code modifications at the application layer. DW-003 includes a portable driver framework supporting GPIO, SPI, I2C, CAN, and Ethernet interfaces, a standardized diagnostic data logging and reporting system compliant with ISO 14229 (Unified Diagnostic Services), and a remote diagnostics communication interface enabling over-the-air (OTA) diagnostic queries and firmware status reporting. The module also implements VMS-originated self-test routines for adaptive mobility hardware verification during vehicle startup sequences."
                ]
            ]
